# Docker build context for the ussdgw images.
#
# The context is the repository root, so this file keeps everything that must NOT
# enter a layer out of it. Without it, `docker build` would ship the whole
# workspace — including 290 dependency jars under dist/lib, local H2 databases,
# runtime logs and the operator's configs.
#
# Only these are needed for the runtime image:
#   dist/ussdgw-app.jar, dist/quarkus-run.jar, dist/lib/, dist/quarkus/,
#   dist/app/html/, dist/run.sh
# (see docker/ussdgw/Dockerfile — it COPYs only those paths).

# Build outputs and the packaged tree.
target/
dist/lib/
dist/quarkus/
dist/app/
dist/configs/
dist/data/
dist/logs/
dist/.baked-db-kind
dist/*.jar

# Source is mounted at runtime in the builder; never bake it into the image.
src/
*.tar.gz
*.tar

# Git and editor noise.
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/
*.iml
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursor/

# Secrets and operator state — must never enter a layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
configs/digicom/
build/digicom-secrets-*.txt
build/.digicom-rotate.env
**/application-digicom.properties
**/ss7-digicom*.json

# Runtime state.
data/
logs/
*.log
*.pcap
*.mv
*.gz

# Docs and tooling that the images do not need.
docs/
docker/README.md
tools/ss7-simulator/
tools/as-node/